---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
---

<Base
  title="Medical disclaimer"
  description="The limits of this website's educational mental health information and where to find support."
>
  <div class="container narrow section" data-legal-review="pending">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Before you read</p><h1>
        Information, with clear limits.
      </h1><p>Last updated 6 November 2026.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="callout">
        Draft medical disclaimer — legal review is pending. The owner must
        confirm the final wording before public launch.
      </p>
      <h2>General education only</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} shares general information about psychology and everyday wellbeing.
        It does not offer medical advice, diagnosis, therapy, treatment, or a professional
        relationship with a reader. It is not a substitute for advice or care from
        a qualified professional.
      </p>
      <h2>Your circumstances matter</h2>
      <p>
        A page cannot consider your health, history, relationships, or living
        conditions. An idea that helps one person may not fit another. You can
        leave a suggestion that does not feel suitable.
      </p>
      <p>
        For symptoms, treatment, medication, or personal care, speak with an
        appropriately qualified professional. Do not delay seeking care, stop
        medication, or change prescribed treatment because of something you read
        here.
      </p>
      <h2>No promise of results or review</h2>
      <p>
        We do not promise that reading or trying an idea will prevent, improve,
        or resolve a mental health condition. Sample articles await human
        editorial review. A reference link, author attribution, or date does not
        mean a clinician has reviewed an article. Any review status must be
        stated accurately.
      </p>
      <h2>Urgent support</h2>
      <p>
        This website does not monitor requests for help. If you or someone else
        is in immediate danger, contact local emergency services or go to the
        nearest emergency department. See <a href="/get-help/">Get Help</a> for global
        support directories and the current status of checked contacts.
      </p>
      <h2>External services</h2>
      <p>
        References, support directories, newsletter providers, and media
        platforms are outside services. We do not control their information,
        availability, privacy practices, or the support they offer. A link does
        not mean that a service endorses this website.
      </p>
      <h2>Sources and corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Sources need human checking and can change. Read our <a
          href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a
        > and <a href="/content-guidelines/">content guidelines</a> for the intended
        standards. A working correction contact must be provided before public launch.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
